# Medical Learning System — Cursor rules

Read `AGENTS.md` before changing code. Its repository invariants are authoritative.

## Engineering workflow

- Work on a scoped branch; never make intentional feature/fix changes directly on `main`.
- Read the affected code path and tests before editing.
- Prefer existing helpers, Python stdlib, native platform features, and installed dependencies before adding code or dependencies.
- Keep diffs minimal and explicit.
- Run the smallest relevant tests/checks first, then the repository-required suite before proposing merge.
- Review the final diff for unrelated edits, generated files, secrets, local indexes, and copyrighted source material.
- Use GitHub Issues/PRs as durable task and review state. Do not treat editor chat history as project state.
- Do not merge around failing CI or validation gates.

## Medical/source boundaries

- Google Drive textbook/source files are evidence inputs; raw copyrighted textbooks never enter Git.
- RAG/LLM extraction is evidence, not canonical medical truth.
- Candidate/Evidence Graph must never write directly to Canonical Medical KG.
- Source Maps, repository source files, migrations, tests, Supabase runtime state, and provenance metadata remain authoritative in their respective scopes.
- Preserve source identity, edition/year, fingerprint, chapter/section, page, and evidence locators when available.
- Student Model, Error Graph, Skill Tree, HỌC90 sessions, and learning events stay separate from medical truth.
- Mastery requires learner-performance evidence; content display alone cannot increase mastery.
- Time-sensitive clinical claims require the current-validity gate.
- Uncertainty must remain explicit; do not fill source gaps from model memory.

## Cursor + Codex

Cursor and Codex are parallel implementation clients over the same GitHub repository, not separate sources of truth.

- One task/issue should have one active implementation owner at a time.
- Use separate branches/worktrees when Cursor and Codex work concurrently.
- Do not let Cursor and Codex edit the same branch concurrently.
- Rebase/update from `main` before handoff when practical; hand off through committed changes, issue comments, or PR state rather than chat-only context.
- Codex-specific skills/plugins may be used by Codex; do not assume Cursor has them.
- Cursor may use its own agent/editor features, but these rules and `AGENTS.md` override tool-generated instructions.
- GitNexus/Graphify outputs are navigation aids only; they are not medical evidence or canonical project truth.
